# Security baseline

Baseline org standard for all services and frontends in this repository.

**VAPT addendum:** `docs/agents-v0/security/vapt-prevention-guardrails.md` · Team rules: `vapt-spring.mdc`, `vapt-webapp.mdc`, `vapt-pr-review.mdc`

**Verify gate.** Always-on findings are F4, F8, F9, and F10. An applicable miss is Critical. F1–F3 and F5–F7 are regression checks for the surface the diff touches. HIGH and MEDIUM block merge on that surface. LOW blocks only when the diff makes the issue exploitable.

Traceability to OWASP ASVS 5.0.0 lives in `docs/agents-v0/compliance-matrix.md`.

---

## 1. Authentication

| Requirement | Standard |
|-------------|----------|
| Protocol | OAuth 2.0 / OpenID Connect (Okta) or JWT Bearer — no custom auth schemes |
| Session model | Stateless JWT for REST APIs; document if cookie sessions are used |
| Browser session | Access token in memory. Refresh token in an HttpOnly, Secure, SameSite cookie |
| MFA | Required for admin/backoffice portals |
| Step-up | Required for actions the requirements artifact marks sensitive |
| Logout | Drop the in-memory access token, expire the refresh cookie, blacklist the server token, clear other client state, revoke the IdP session where SSO applies |
| Token blacklist | Fail-closed on infrastructure errors — never accept revoked tokens when Redis is unavailable |
| Account recovery | Login and account-recovery responses are identical for known and unknown users |
| Dev bypass | Static dev tokens and `permit-all` **local only** — never in lab/SIT/UAT/prod |

**JWT validation** before any claim is trusted:

- Allowlist the signature algorithm. Reject `none`.
- Validate `iss`, `aud`, `exp`, and `nbf`.
- Accept `kid` only for known keys. Ignore `jku`, `x5u`, and `jwk` unless that URL is on the issuer allowlist.
- Keep the access-token lifetime short.
- Rotate refresh tokens. Reuse of an already-used refresh token revokes that token family.
- Authorization identity is the validated `sub` (with `iss` when more than one issuer is configured).

**CSRF:** cookie sessions need CSRF tokens or SameSite + framework defaults; Bearer-only SPAs omit CSRF but must not put tokens in query strings.

---

## 2. Authorization

| Requirement | Standard |
|-------------|----------|
| Model | RBAC or ABAC; least privilege |
| Enforcement | **Server-side on every endpoint** — filter-level `authenticated()` alone is insufficient for admin APIs |
| Annotations | `@PreAuthorize` (or equivalent) on every controller method that mutates or exposes sensitive data |
| Object scope | For every `{id}` path, confirm the principal may access **that** instance (tenant/org/user). A role check is not proof of ownership |
| Field scope | Writes bind through a request DTO that rejects unknown properties. `@JsonIgnore` on sensitive response fields |
| Client UI | Hiding nav links is **not** authorization — enforce in BFF, `+layout.server.ts`, or service layer |
| Trust boundary | Never trust client-supplied role/permission headers or query params |
| Fail closed | When the policy or entitlement service errors, deny the request |
| Bypass flags | No `MethodSecurityBypass`-style flags that disable authz in shared environments |

- **Authentication vs authorization:** verify caller identity (JWT, session, mTLS) at the edge; propagate principal to services. Enforce **RBAC/ABAC** and **resource-scoped** checks in the **service that owns the data** — not only at the gateway.
- **BOLA / IDOR:** the retest is a same-role peer, not only a missing admin role (VAPT F8).

