## 11. Compliance & Review

- Identify applicable regulations (GDPR, BSP, Data Privacy Act, internal GXI policies) per system
- When the system stores regulated personal data, apply §3 (at rest), §7 (TLS), and §12 (audit events)
- Security review required for: auth changes, new upload endpoints, RBAC changes, new public routes, and any `{id}` path
- VAPT retest criteria: see `docs/agents-v0/security/vapt-prevention-guardrails.md` (Retest Matrix)

---

## 12. Security audit events

Required events: authentication success and failure, logout, authorization denial, token revocation, admin mutation, upload accept and reject.

Each event includes the correlation id, principal, action, and result. Dynamic values use `Encode.forJava()` in Java (or the equivalent elsewhere). The event does not contain a token, password, or secret.

A diff that adds or changes one of those actions ships the event in the same change (VAPT F10).
